# TODO — opm status
File: opm/audit/todo.oot
Date: 2026-09-04.

The kill list from zero-trust.oot is executed. This file is status,
not a description of today's bugs.

Stay in opm/. Do not add subcommands. Version is the git tag.
No VERSION file. No extra .md. Files of product code <= 256 lines.

## Landed

- Help names equal `cli/main.oo` dispatch names.
- `sbom` calls `run_ooda_pm_sbom`. Not an alias of audit.
- `cmd_more.oo` gone. Helpers are not commands:
  catalog, argv, slurp, vendor_pick, git_clone, reg_fetch.
- Argv rest: init/bot/publish read index 0. `pm_argv_self_test` asserts it.
- `OODA_COMPILER` only. No `bin/oodac` or `ooda/oodac_bin`.
- No `sh -c` in cli/ or registry/. Git/curl/minisign need
  `OODA_GIT` / `OODA_CURL` / `OODA_MINISIGN`.
- No `../registry` fallback. No `$HOME` via shell.
- `cmd_add.oo` split (add_select, add_lock). `core/core.oo` is
  `core/semver.oo`. Starter manifest has no `min_pin=v0.210.0`.
- User-facing print is `opm <cmd>:`, not `ooda <cmd>:`.
- Docs and examples match the live lock line and `opm <subcommand>`.
- `scripts/verify.oo` refuses VERSION, cmd_more, host_build, core.oo,
  compiler fallbacks, and sh -c.
- `scripts/test.oo` double-runs `oodac check`. `oodac run` waits on
  a compiler that does not look for `./bin/oodac_bin.core`.
- CI is auto-release only until `OODA_COMPILER` is on the runner.

Keep: resolve/, lock lines, policy/caps, qa proofs that assert.
The unique move is cap-aware resolve.

## Git ingest pin (landed)

`origin=git` needs a hex `commit=` (7+ digits). `main` / `HEAD` refuse.
Clone needs `url=` + `OODA_GIT` + allow-list. After the name is in
the lock, `sha256=` is required.

## Blocked on an oodac binary (Gemini)

- Typecheck `cli/main.oo` and `cli/catalog.oo`
  (`import "std/..."` from under `cli/`).
- `qa/extract_proof.oo` (`launch/std/sec/untrusted.oo`).
- Flip `scripts/test.oo` from `check` to `run`.
- CI test job before auto-release.

## Not this repo

- New subcommands.
- Token / MCP / LSP.
- Inventing a NetCap type.
- Changing the `opm/std` symlink topology.

## Done means (still)

Help equals dispatch. No sh -c. No VERSION file.
No bin/oodac fallback. sbom is sbom. Files <= 256 lines.
When the oodac binary ships, the blocked list is the next gate.
